# The state is a build artefact and is never committed.
#
# **A committed snapshot is a number nobody checked**, and every step of the build reports
# success while it happens. This page is built from what the collector read, so the file
# that records what it read is not source.
src/state/

# A checkout of the repository the page is published from, if there is one.
build/

# **No trailing slash on node_modules, because a symlink is not a directory.**
# A trailing slash matches directories only, and a checkout that reuses its sibling's
# installed packages makes a symlink — so `node_modules/` ignores nothing and a commit
# of a checkout carries a second one into it, several hundred thousand paths.
node_modules
dist/
.astro/

# macOS
.DS_Store
